shape: sequence_diagram

title: Customer app · one journey through the BFF {
  shape: text
  style.font-size: 22
  style.bold: true
  near: top-center
}

# One view, one question: who talks to whom when a customer logs in, lands
# on the summary, pays someone and logs out. The client renders screen
# trees and follows their actions; the BFF holds no banking logic and no
# state of its own but the session; the core is the bank (ADR-0002).

client: App or web client
bff: BFF
core: Core (the bank)

client -> bff: GET /v1/screen/login
bff -> client: login screen
client -> bff: POST /v1/login (customer ID, password)
bff -> core: Authenticate
core -> bff: customer
bff -> bff: create session (token for the app, cookie for the web)
bff -> client: 303 to /v1/screen/home (web) · token + home screen (app)
client -> bff: GET /v1/screen/home
bff -> core: Customer · Accounts · Transactions
core -> bff: position and recent movements
bff -> client: home screen tree (summary)
client -> bff: tap "Pay someone" · GET /v1/screen/pay
bff -> client: pay screen (form)
client -> bff: POST /v1/pay (to, amount, reference)
bff -> core: Transfer
core -> bff: payment on record
bff -> client: payment-sent screen
client -> bff: GET /v1/screen/accounts (session idle too long)
bff -> client: 401 · signed-out screen with notice
client -> bff: POST /v1/logout
bff -> bff: revoke session
bff -> client: signed-out screen
